      "abstract": "Can humanism be post-colonial? What is Africana Philosophy? Who is Lewis Gordon? This paper presents some typical elements of the Jamaican philosopher Lewis Gordon\u2019s thought and relates it to the field of Africana Philosophy. For this purpose, it seeks to delineate its theoretical influences and the usage of concepts, such as theodicy, bad faith and reason to understand anti-black racism. In this sense, the following argument pivots on Lewis Gordon\u2019s singular contribution to different areas of study, especially political philosophy, social sciences and the humanities. Keywords: Lewis Gordon; Africana Philosophy; Post-colonial Humanism; Existential Phenomenology.",
